  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "A customer service representative resolves a caller\u2019s issue with a $45%$ chance during each minute of a call. The call continues until the issue is resolved. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability that it will take exactly $5$ minutes to resolve the issue is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of minutes until the representative resolves the issue. Since the chance of resolving the issue in any given minute is $45%,$ the number of minutes until the issue is resolved can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success\n\n$$\np=45%=\\frac{45}{100}=0.45.\n$$\n\nSo, $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(0.45).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.45)^{x-1}(0.45) \\\\  & =(0.55)^{x-1}(0.45)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the representative will resolve the issue for the first time in the $5$th minute is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =f(5) \\\\  & =(0.55)^{5-1}(0.45) \\\\  & =(0.55)^{4}(0.45) \\\\  & \u22480.041,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
